🚀 Follow-up: O(1) Space (IMPORTANT)

Now the interview-level optimization.

🧠 Idea
Instead of building strings:
👉 Traverse from right to left
👉 Skip characters that should be deleted

🔥 Intuition
'#' = skip next character
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
✅ Code (O(1) space)

class Solution(object):
    def backspaceCompare(self, s, t):

        i = len(s) - 1
        j = len(t) - 1

        skipS = 0
        skipT = 0

        while i >= 0 or j >= 0:

            while i >= 0:
                if s[i] == "#":
                    skipS += 1
                    i -= 1
                elif skipS > 0:
                    skipS -= 1
                    i -= 1
                else:
                    break

            while j >= 0:
                if t[j] == "#":
                    skipT += 1
                    j -= 1
                elif skipT > 0:
                    skipT -= 1
                    j -= 1
                else:
                    break

            if i >= 0 and j >= 0:
                if s[i] != t[j]:
                    return False
            elif i >= 0 or j >= 0:
                return False

            i -= 1
            j -= 1

        return True
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🧠 Core Idea Reminder

Go from RIGHT → LEFT
"#" = skip characters

We maintain:
i → pointer for s
j → pointer for t
skipS → how many chars to skip in s
skipT → how many chars to skip in t

